a viewer wrote in via email should they  do jury duty  i think this is a great question and the  answer to that is unequivocally yes  number one not only is it your civic  duty to make sure that  the government doesn't overreach and  that you protect everyone's rights which  in turn protects everyone else's rights  but it's also an incredibly fascinating  experience every time i've done jury  duty  i am lucky to be there and here's one  secret that you might actually not know  about jury duty which is that in many  jurisdictions  the judge is given a list of the jurors  who gets  paid for their time on jury duty and  often judges bend over backwards to make  sure that people who aren't compensated  for their time on the jury  are not selected because that can be a  huge hardship for the jurors  but if you are compensated for your time  by your employer then you're more likely  to be on jury duty and of course  it makes it more likely that you can  fulfill your duties so in answer to your  question yes you should do jury duty so  i'll see you  in court
 

